{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "**Chasing Cherry Blossoms: A Weekend in Tokyo and Kyoto**\n\nMy recent trip to Japan was a whirlwind of ancient traditions meeting futuristic innovation. Starting in Tokyo, the energy was electric. I navigated the neon-lit streets of Shinjuku and marveled at the orderly chaos of the Shibuya Crossing. The food was unforgettable; from steaming bowls of ramen in tiny alleyway shops to the precision of a sushi Omakase in Ginza, every bite was perfection.\n\nLeaving the capital, I took the Shinkansen to Kyoto, where the pace slowed dramatically. The contrast was striking. Wandering through the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove felt like stepping into another world, the green stalks swaying silently above. The highlight, however, was the golden Kinkaku-ji Temple reflecting in its pond, a vision of serene beauty that stayed with me long after I left.\n\nOne moment stands out above all: watching the sunrise over Fushimi Inari Taisha. The thousands of vermilion torii gates stretching up the mountain created a path that seemed to lead straight to the heavens. It was quiet, spiritual, and profoundly moving.\n\nJapan's unique blend of hyper-modernity and deep-rooted history is unmatched. Whether you are sipping matcha in a centuries-old tea house or exploring a high-tech subway system, the country offers an experience that engages all the senses. If you haven't been yet, put it on your list immediately. You won't regret it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.29092026}, {"token": "Ch", "logprob": -0.23610641}, {"token": "asing", "logprob": -1.1128038}, {"token": " Cherry", "logprob": -0.009600563}, {"token": " Bloss", "logprob": -0.0004985383}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ":", "logprob": -0.91601026}, {"token": " A", "logprob": -0.39848083}, {"token": " Weekend", "logprob": -0.2108005}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -2.384186e-07}, {"token": " Tokyo", "l